    pr_ref:  # e783
    description: "FOUND while landing INV-kaduh's C/C++ io_mode producer, as the control on the\ncpp arm: the mode stamp landed correctly and the boundary did not move, because\ncpp's fopen never reaches the catalogue AT ALL.\n\nTHE PRODUCER CONVENTION. cpp.py pre-collects every `#include <...>` in the file\nand, for an unresolved call, sets the dst's module slot to the COMMA-JOINED\nlist of all of them (cpp.py:1374, `module_hint = \",\".join(system_includes)`):\n\n    cpp:stdio.h,vector,string:0-0:fopen:unresolved\n\nIts own comment states the intended contract -- \"the semantics is 'this call\ncould be from any of the included headers'; downstream consumers may split the\nmodule_hint on commas if they need per-header resolution.\"\n\nTHE CONSUMER DOES NOT EXIST. `IoBoundaryCatalog.lookup_with_module` never\nsplits. It hands the whole joined string to `_module_matches`, which is EXACT\n(deliberately -- a prefix rule was wrong in three languages at once), so a\nmulti-include file matches nothing. A SINGLE-include file does not match either,\nbecause the slot keeps the FILENAME while `c.yaml` declares the header STEM:\n`stdio.h` != `stdio`, and `<cstdio>` is a third spelling again.\n\n    _module_matches(\"stdio\", \"stdio.h\")  -> False\n    lookup_with_module(\"fopen\", \"stdio.h\")  -> None\n    lookup_with_module(\"fopen\", \"stdio\")    -> IoPrimitive(fs_write, stdio, fopen)\n\nMEASURED on ~/ALL_REPOS/whole_bunch_of_repos/whisper.cpp, real repo, production\nclassifiers, call edges only:\n\n    cpp call edges                                 82,547\n    matched to the catalogue TODAY                      6\n    unmatched despite carrying a module hint       45,843\n      of which the hint is comma-joined            43,849\n    recoverable by splitting the hint + .h stem        80   (6 -> 86, 14x)\n\nThe recovered 80 are not marginal -- they are the security-relevant surface:\n\n    16  stdlib.getenv        [env_read]     <- a taint SOURCE, not just a boundary\n    15  stdio.fclose         [fs_write]\n     8/5/4/3  stdio.ftell/fseek/fread/fopen\n     3/2/2/1/1  sys/socket.bind/connect/socket/listen/send/recv  [net_*]\n     1/1/1/2  unistd.fork, unistd.execvp, sys/wait.waitpid/wait  [subprocess]\n     1  sys/stat.mkdir       [fs_write]\n\nSo C++'s ENTIRE network, subprocess and env-read surface is invisible to\nio-boundaries and to every taint source/sink derived from it.\n\nWHY THIS IS FILED SEPARATELY FROM INV-kaduh. Different invariant (a catalogued\ncall site must REACH its entry regardless of module SPELLING -- INV-linub's\nclass, in INV-fokik's slot-shape costume), different fix site, and the fix has\nreal blast radius: splitting on commas and stripping a `.h` stem changes module\nmatching for every language that shares `lookup_with_module`. The freeze rule is\nminimal, independently revertable PRs, so INV-kaduh ships the producer and this\nships the consumer.\n\nFIX SHAPE (not costed). In `lookup_with_module`, treat a comma-joined hint as a\nDISJUNCTION -- try each part, then each part's header stem. Open question the\nfix must answer rather than assume: a disjunction weakens the module filter's\nfalse-positive guard, since a file including 12 headers gets 12 chances to\nmatch a short name. Whether that is acceptable is exactly what `ambiguous_names`\nand the F3 kind gate were built to bound, and it must be MEASURED on the\nfalse-positive side, not argued.\n\nNOT SWEPT: whether the `<cstdio>` -> `stdio` C++-convention mapping is worth\ncarrying, and whether any other analyzer joins multiple hints into one slot."  # e783
    fields:  # e783
      statement: "A catalogued I/O call site must reach its catalogue entry regardless of how the analyzer spells the module slot. VIOLATED for cpp: cpp.py sets the module slot to the comma-joined list of the file's system includes and keeps the header FILENAME, while c.yaml declares header STEMS, so lookup_with_module's exact match refuses every one. Measured on whisper.cpp: 6 of 86 reachable primitives matched; the 80 missed include getenv (env_read source), socket/connect/send/recv/bind/listen, and fork/execvp/waitpid."  # e783
      root_cause: "cpp.py:1374 emits module_hint=','.join(system_includes) and documents that 'downstream consumers may split the module_hint on commas' -- a producer contract with no consumer. lookup_with_module hands the joined string to _module_matches, which is exact by design (a prefix rule was wrong in three languages at once), so a multi-include file matches nothing; a single-include file also misses because the slot carries 'stdio.h' and the catalogue declares 'stdio'."  # e783
